POSTS = [
    ('Which window', '<p>South windows are bright and hot: cacti, olives, pilea. East windows are gentle: ferns, calathea, pothos. North windows are for the tough ones: snake plants and the fern that forgives you.</p><p>Most plants die of kindness. Water when the top two centimetres are dry, not on a schedule.</p>', 'Houseplants on a bright windowsill with morning sun through the glass.'),
    ('Sowing in March', '<p>Tomatoes and chillies indoors on a warm windowsill now. Peas and broad beans straight into the ground. Lettuce in a tray under cover, then out in April.</p><p>Label everything. You will not remember.</p>', 'Seed trays with small seedlings and wooden labels on a sunny potting bench.'),
    ('Sharpen your tools', '<p>A sharp spade cuts roots instead of tearing them, and a sharp hoe skims weeds without effort. Ten strokes with a file along the bevel, once a month, is all it takes.</p><p>Wipe the steel with an oily rag before winter. Ash handles want a little linseed.</p>', 'A hand sharpening a spade blade with a file on a workbench in a shed.'),
]
